WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.630
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Writing Skills.

2
00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:08.340
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:13.870
Unit nineteen: Writing Summaries. Today you will summarise a text in your own words.

4
00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:16.601
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:17.567 --> 00:00:21.252
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.117 --> 00:00:22.932
Summary.

7
00:00:23.917 --> 00:00:26.253
Summary means a short version of a text.

8
00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:28.350
Write a short summary.

9
00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:31.568
Your turn. Say: Summary.

10
00:00:34.433 --> 00:00:35.272
Summary.

11
00:00:36.017 --> 00:00:37.122
Main idea.

12
00:00:38.117 --> 00:00:40.824
Main idea means the most important point.

13
00:00:41.417 --> 00:00:42.836
Find the main idea.

14
00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:46.439
Your turn. Say: Main idea.

15
00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:50.464
Main idea.

16
00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:52.183
Key point.

17
00:00:53.183 --> 00:00:55.833
Key point means an important piece of information.

18
00:00:56.417 --> 00:00:57.975
List the key points.

19
00:00:58.583 --> 00:01:01.108
Your turn. Say: Key point.

20
00:01:03.967 --> 00:01:04.875
Key point.

21
00:01:05.617 --> 00:01:06.722
Paraphrase.

22
00:01:07.717 --> 00:01:10.541
Paraphrase means to say something in other words.

23
00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:12.627
Paraphrase the sentence.

24
00:01:13.217 --> 00:01:16.357
Your turn. Say: Paraphrase.

25
00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:20.387
Paraphrase.

26
00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:22.012
Omit.

27
00:01:23.017 --> 00:01:24.680
Omit means to leave out.

28
00:01:25.283 --> 00:01:27.178
Omit the small details.

29
00:01:27.783 --> 00:01:30.227
Your turn. Say: Omit.

30
00:01:33.067 --> 00:01:33.894
Omit.

31
00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:35.872
Concise.

32
00:01:36.883 --> 00:01:38.813
Concise means short and clear.

33
00:01:39.417 --> 00:01:40.557
Be concise.

34
00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:43.849
Your turn. Say: Concise.

35
00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:47.806
Concise.

36
00:01:48.550 --> 00:01:49.632
Objective.

37
00:01:50.617 --> 00:01:53.940
Objective means not influenced by personal feelings.

38
00:01:54.550 --> 00:01:56.190
Keep the summary objective.

39
00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:59.679
Your turn. Say: Objective.

40
00:02:02.533 --> 00:02:03.465
Objective.

41
00:02:04.217 --> 00:02:05.299
Source.

42
00:02:06.283 --> 00:02:08.573
Source means where information comes from.

43
00:02:09.183 --> 00:02:10.417
Name the source.

44
00:02:11.017 --> 00:02:13.414
Your turn. Say: Source.

45
00:02:16.267 --> 00:02:17.268
Source.

46
00:02:18.067 --> 00:02:22.089
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:24.799
Visal, how do I write a summary?

48
00:02:25.883 --> 00:02:35.179
Read the text and find the main idea and key points. Then write them in your own words. A summary is much shorter than the original.

49
00:02:36.283 --> 00:02:37.702
What should I leave out?

50
00:02:38.817 --> 00:02:44.766
Omit small details, examples and your own opinion. A summary must stay objective.

51
00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:47.107
How do I begin?

52
00:02:48.217 --> 00:02:56.488
Name the source and the author. For example, According to the article by Dara Kim, schools should start later.

53
00:02:57.633 --> 00:02:59.064
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:59.917 --> 00:03:02.636
Grammar focus: Reporting phrases.

55
00:03:02.936 --> 00:03:04.158
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:07.871
According to the article, schools should start later.

57
00:03:08.783 --> 00:03:11.607
The author states that sleep helps students learn.

58
00:03:12.567 --> 00:03:18.481
Begin a summary with according to or the author states that. Use your own words and omit small details.

59
00:03:19.217 --> 00:03:23.100
Be careful! Don't say: The author state that sleep helps.

60
00:03:25.033 --> 00:03:27.892
Say: The author states that sleep helps.

61
00:03:28.192 --> 00:03:29.599
Add s after author.

62
00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:33.296
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:35.670
Summarising an Article.

64
00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:39.107
Maly reads an article about school start times.

65
00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:42.901
She underlines the main idea and three key points.

66
00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:46.991
She omits the examples and writes in her own words.

67
00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:52.298
Her summary begins, According to the article, students need more sleep.

68
00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:55.718
It stays short and does not give her opinion.

69
00:03:56.833 --> 00:04:00.614
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:03.380
A summary is a blank version.

71
00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:07.066
A, loud. B, short. C, long.

72
00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:12.507
The answer is B: short.

73
00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:15.429
Omit means to leave blank.

74
00:04:15.729 --> 00:04:18.825
A, in. B, on. C, out.

75
00:04:22.367 --> 00:04:24.169
The answer is C: out.

76
00:04:25.317 --> 00:04:27.316
A paraphrase uses your own blank.

77
00:04:27.616 --> 00:04:30.643
A, words. B, money. C, keys.

78
00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:36.060
The answer is A: words.

79
00:04:37.217 --> 00:04:39.309
Objective means no personal blank.

80
00:04:39.609 --> 00:04:42.485
A, time. B, opinion. C, name.

81
00:04:46.033 --> 00:04:48.149
The answer is B: opinion.

82
00:04:49.283 --> 00:04:51.155
Maly summarises an blank.

83
00:04:51.455 --> 00:04:54.714
A, engine. B, orange. C, article.

84
00:04:58.267 --> 00:05:00.487
The answer is C: article.

85
00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:04.643
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:05.483 --> 00:05:07.320
How do you summarise a text?

87
00:05:16.117 --> 00:05:17.780
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:29.744
I find the main idea and the key points. I write them in my own words and omit small details and examples. I keep my summary short and objective and name the source.

89
00:05:30.044 --> 00:05:31.649
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:32.550 --> 00:05:36.514
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and reporting phrases.

91
00:05:36.814 --> 00:05:40.883
Today's value is precision. Choose your words and numbers with care.

92
00:05:41.183 --> 00:05:43.731
See you in Unit twenty. Goodbye!

93
00:05:44.031 --> 00:05:47.240
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

